+## 0.7 stabilization boundary
+
+The 0.7.9 line stabilizes the current supervised path. Agentplane owns task state, routing,
+authority, verification, repository operations, and closeout. A semantic agent receives one bounded
+episode at a time. Completed tasks expose provider token usage as informational telemetry when the
+provider reports it, or an explicit partial/unavailable state when it does not. Input, cached-input,
+output, reasoning, and total token fields keep their subset relationships; cached-input and
+reasoning tokens are not added to the total again. Token caps are disabled by default and do not
+depend on API billing, credits, purchases, or account classification. Non-token safety limits remain
+active.
+
+The preregistered M01 pilot does not establish a token-efficiency result for 0.7.9. Its first
+15-attempt campaign failed provider schema admission. A schema-corrected 15-attempt campaign
+observed token usage for every attempt, but a task-entry mismatch and a path-verifier defect left no
+quality-equivalent verified pair. Agentplane retains both campaigns and makes no performance or
+safety claim from their raw totals. A future measurement must use a new preregistered campaign; it
+must not replace or selectively retry these attempts.
+
+Later releases retain their own boundaries:
+
+| Release | Deferred task ids       | Boundary                                                                |
+| ------- | ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| 0.7.10  | `BP-01` through `BP-31` | Retire Blueprint runtime ownership only after each consumer is rebound. |
+| 0.7.11  | `LC-01` through `LC-24` | Converge lifecycle execution on one Kernel-backed coordinator.          |
+| 0.7.12  | `PL-01` through `PL-12` | Qualify optional planning while preserving required planning semantics. |
+| 0.7.13  | `RC-01` through `RC-18` | Introduce and qualify the formal Recipe contract.                       |
+| 0.7.14  | `EV-01` through `EV-13` | Qualify a narrow review-omission rule before activation.                |
+
+Adaptive or shadow review classification is not part of the default 0.7.9 path and is not a 0.7.9
+release dependency. Its first read-only diagnostic is deferred to `EV-04`; independent review
+remains required in 0.7.9. Publication remains a separate operator action after exact-head local and
+hosted verification.
+
